        "afterFontSize": 36,
        "ratio": 2
      },
      {
        "index": 47,
        "tag": "P",
        "text": "Most teams that have built guardrails believe they have governance. They have not, and the gap is expensive.",
        "fontSize": 16,
        "afterFontSize": 32,
        "ratio": 2
      },
      {
        "index": 48,
        "tag": "P",
        "text": "A guardrail is a mechanism: an output filter, a rate limit, a system prompt, an approval step. An authority model is the",
        "fontSize": 16,
        "afterFontSize": 32,
        "ratio": 2
      },
      {
        "index": 49,
        "tag": "P",
        "text": "Every bank already runs this distinction without thinking about it. Its delegation of authority says a relationship mana",
